example.paragraph:
The line through $\textbf{0}$ and $\textbf{p}$ has the equation $y = (b/a)t$ for $t$ real. That line intersects $S$ where $t$ satisfies $(b/a)t = t^{2}\text{,}$ that is, when $t = b/a\text{.}$ Thus, $\textbf{p}$ is on the line segment from $0$ to $\begin{bmatrix}
        {b/a} \\
        {b^{2}/a^{2}}
        \end{bmatrix}$, which shows that Figure 3 is correct.

